@@ -6,3 +6,16 @@ package holds the order book, in TypeScript; the shop's website and its staff to
 `src/index.ts`.
 
 Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## Discount codes
+
+An order takes one discount code at most, given with `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`; a second code replaces the first.
+Codes are not case-sensitive and surrounding spaces are ignored.
+
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € or more.
+
+The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before any discount. An
+unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with a message saying why, and the order is left as it was.
+`totals(orderNumber)` shows the discount as `discountCents` (0 without a code), and `totalCents` is items minus
+discount plus shipping.
